      "publication_year": 2014,
      "publication_date": "2014-08-11",
      "abstract": "My fieldwork among HIV vaccine researchers, activists, and funders has led me to suggest that humanity\u2014when it was first conceived of in the late eighteenth century\u2014emerged as a plan, a plan for how to establish a future anticipated in the present. The powerful implication of this fieldwork-based suggestion is that what humanity is\u2014or if it is at all\u2014depends on the available humanity plans. I argue in this essay that we are currently seeing the emergence of a new\u2014a biological\u2014humanity plan, and I wish to make visible that\u2014and how\u2014this biological humanity plan has outgrown, conceptually as well as institutionally, older humanity plans. I also hope to make comprehensible the massive\u2014intellectual as well as political\u2014challenge this emergence poses.",
